---
description: Keep project documentation free of dates and timestamps
alwaysApply: true
---

- Do not add calendar dates or wall-clock timestamps to documentation prose, headings, captions, tables, or preparation/update/research notes.
- Use versions, commit hashes, and evidence references for provenance in documentation.
- Keep cited source URLs accurate, including date-containing paths when required by the source.
- Keep required runtime time fields and original machine-readable benchmark provenance separate from documentation prose.
- Check documentation for dates and timestamps before committing.
